From: Jianfeng Liu <Jianfeng.Liu@cixtech.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 19:29:03 +0800
Subject: drm/panthor: Sky1 (CIXH5000) ACPI bring-up

Bring the driver up on the Sky1 SoC when probed via ACPI:

- Sky1 detection via ACPI HID (panthor_is_sky1) and power-on through a
  raw SMC SCMI POWER_STATE_SET call to TFA, which also configures IDM
  non-secure access; without it GPU register access raises SError.
- MMIO resource mapping: resource 0 is RCSU, resource 1 is GPU registers.
- clk / clk-stacks lookup under the vendor clock names exposed by ACPI,
  optional reset control, and the Sky1 power-on sequence (IP reset +
  Q-channel clock gating).
- IRQ lookup by index under ACPI (vs byname under DT).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
